       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/010c261cd3ec86eb2b15db9e0bd1f9fa?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMK-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/010c261cd3ec86eb2b15db9e0bd1f9fa?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMK-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/010c261cd3ec86eb2b15db9e0bd1f9fa?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMK-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael B. Klein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fac9ba4-ab49-400b-81c4-9ce0204129bf",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Requesting a particular content disposition will have to happen through the URL itself, as opposed to a request header, since it will have to be usable within a <tt>rel</tt>, <tt>src</tt>, or <tt>href</tt>.</p>\n\n<p>Possible resolutions:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Change the default behavior to <tt>content-disposition: inline</tt> and add an <tt>fcr:attachment</tt> URL extension (similar to <tt>fcr:metadata</tt>) to force the download</li>\n\t<li>Keep the existing default behavior, and add an <tt>fcr:content</tt> URL extension to allow inline retrieval</li>\n\t<li>Similar to the above, but use a query string parameter (e.g., <tt>inline=true</tt>) to alter the response</li>\n</ol>\n",
     "created": "17/Nov/15 4:02 PM",
     "id": "15847",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11768/comment/15847",
